!!!!!IMPORTANT!!!!!!
Commands including -Dquarkus require quotation marks (as documented here) because for me, they were wrongly interpreted as lifecycle phases otherwise.
All commands were done within IntelliJ local terminal, so other terminals or bash may require to leave the quotation marks away.
Project built and compiled on JDK22. Does not work on JDK25

first of all, please do make sure to use "mvn verify" (and make sure both the pom.xml and pom-docker.xml have been added/ are compiled as maven projects)

command to just run the application in quarkus:
mvn compile quarkus:dev


since the last given docker command (for testing) only worked for me after using all 4 below commands first, please do run them before using the last command as well. I had quite some issues setting up docker, so i really hope it works on another computer as well.

Creating docker image:
docker build -f src/test/docker/Dockerfile --tag myapp:1.0 .
docker run --rm -p 8080:8080 myapp:1.0

running docker:
mvn package
mvn package -Dquarkus.package.jar.type=uber-jar"


Integration testing: (this only worked for me after using mvn package and creating the docker build)
mvn -f pom-docker.xml clean verify "-Dquarkus.http.test-port=8080" "-Dquarkus.http.test-host=localhost"
